**Assessment:** The paper is positioned above the medium band (4-6) due to its genuine contributions — a general unifying framework, resolution of an open conjecture, and unified treatment of 8 GNN families. However, it falls meaningfully below the high band (7+) because: (1) strict inequalities in Corollary 10 are unproved, (2) the cross-order expressivity comparison lacks a formal bridge, and (3) there are no experiments whatsoever. The most directly comparable high-scoring paper (HSKaGOi7Ar, 8.5) earned its score partly through complete, elegant proofs and empirical validation — both of which are absent or incomplete here.

