**Assessment:** After removing the parser-artifact criticisms, the remaining genuine weaknesses are (1) a notation error in Eq. 9, (2) the Genre near-random performance being unexplained, and (3) a mild overclaim about Variant 4 performance. None of these threaten the core contribution. The paper is a solid empirical contribution with a principled design and strong results. It sits clearly above the rejected temporal-graph papers (SIG at 5.0, Todyformer at 4.25) and roughly at the level of TGC (7.33), though slightly below because of the genre mystery and notation issues. I position it at **6.5**, aligned with an accept-poster quality paper: above the borderline, below spotlight.

