**Assessment:** The paper makes a genuinely surprising and well-demonstrated empirical discovery (catastrophic importance of single weight scalars), provides a practically useful identification method and artifact (SW directory), and offers incremental but honest quantization improvements. Its weaknesses — incomplete mechanistic explanation (~58% of quality loss unexplained), comparisons against magnitude-selected rather than sensitivity-selected baselines, and a weak RTN-only baseline for weight quantization — are real but do not invalidate the core finding. The paper is more novel than the SpQR anchor (6.5) in its observation, but less engineering-complete. The rLX7Vyyzus paper (6.0) is the closest analog in scope (LLM outlier analysis → compression application) and received a 6.0 poster. This paper's empirical finding is more striking, but its mechanistic account is less complete. Splitting the difference and accounting for the quantization utility, I place this at **6.5**.

